            <ArticleTitle>A study of the immunofunction in patients of coronary heart disease with the fundamental deficiency and outward excess syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>290-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The fundamental deficiency and outward excess syndrome of coronary heart disease can be classified into Qi Yang deficiency with blood stasis (QYD) and Yin deficiency with blood stasis (YD). The patients showed disturbances in immunofunction manifested as marked increase of serum IgG, CIC, IC-IgG and IC-C3 levels and the percentage of B cells in the peripheral blood, while the percentages of OKT3+, OKT4+ and OKT8+ cells markedly decreased, especially the percentage of OKT8+ cells, resulting in an increase of the ratio of T4/8 and imbalance between TS and TH. The authors deem that the fundamental deficiency of coronary heart disease is related to the low cellular immunity, especially the imbalance between TS and TH cells, while outward excess of coronary heart disease is related to hyperactivity of humoral immunity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
